nterview question? K Closest Points to Origin - Given an array of points wh=
ere points[i] =3D [xi, yi] represents a point on the X-Y plane and an integ=
er k, return the k closest points to the origin (0, 0).

The distance between two points on the X-Y plane is the Euclidean distance =
(i.e., =E2=88=9A(x1 - x2)2 + (y1 - y2)2).

You may return the answer in any order. The answer is guaranteed to be uniq=
ue (except for the order that it is in).

&nbsp;

Example 1:

[https://assets.leetcode.com/uploads/2021/03/03/closestplane1.jpg]


Input: points =3D [[1,3],[-2,2]], k =3D 1
Output: [[-2,2]]
Explanation:
The distance between (1, 3) and the origin is sqrt(10).
The distance between (-2, 2) and the origin is sqrt(8).
Since sqrt(8) &lt; sqrt(10), (-2, 2) is closer to the origin.
We only want the closest k =3D 1 points from the origin, so the answer is j=
ust [[-2,2]].


Example 2:


Input: points =3D [[3,3],[5,-1],[-2,4]], k =3D 2
Output: [[3,3],[-2,4]]
Explanation: The answer [[-2,4],[3,3]] would also be accepted.


&nbsp;

